---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About - Fictional History Archive">
  <div class="mb-12 border-b-2 border-dashed border-archive-border pb-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mb-4">About the Archive</h2>
    <p class="font-sans text-sm text-archive-muted">Declassifying the multiverse, one document at a time.</p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose prose-invert prose-archive max-w-none font-serif leading-relaxed text-archive-paper">
    <p>
      Welcome to the <strong>Fictional History Archive</strong>. Our mission is to catalogue, preserve, and cross-reference timeline anomalies, historical deviations, and multiversal shifts that occur outside the bounds of conventional reality.
    </p>
    <p>
      Established in the wake of the Great Chrono-Schism, the Archive operates independently of any singular reality's governing body. Our archivists work tirelessly to recover microfilm, digital fragments, and hard-copy documents from timelines that have been erased, overwritten, or split.
    </p>
    <h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-8 mb-4">Our Methodology</h3>
    <p>
      Documents within our collection are rigorously authenticated using chronometric dating and quantum signature analysis. However, due to the nature of multiversal drift, some records may contradict one another. We present these findings without bias, allowing researchers to draw their own conclusions regarding the true nature of historical events.
    </p>
    <div class="bg-archive-surface border-l-4 border-archive-accent p-4 my-6">
      <p class="font-sans text-sm m-0 italic">
        "History is written by the victors, but truth is recorded by those who survive the timeline collapse."
      </p>
      <p class="font-sans text-xs mt-2 text-archive-muted text-right uppercase">
        — The First Archivist (Identity Redacted)
      </p>
    </div>
    <h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-8 mb-4">Access Classification</h3>
    <p>
      The materials presented on this public-facing terminal represent only a fraction of our total collection. Level 4 and higher clearances are required for access to predictive timelines, paradox documentation, and documents concerning entities originating from outside the local multiverse cluster.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
